\section{Public classes}{

These classes are styling hooks: \code{.mascot} (the whole mascot),
\code{.mascot-status} (status text), \code{.mascot-bubble} (speech panel),
\code{.mascot-menu} (menu panel) and \code{.mascot-tooltip} (tooltip panel).
Other classes and all \verb{--_mascot-*} properties are private and may change.
Use \code{\link[=mascot_size]{mascot_size()}} and \code{\link[=mascot_placement]{mascot_placement()}} for size and position.
}

\section{Public custom properties}{

Set these on \code{.mascot}, an individual mascot's id, or an ancestor such as
\verb{:root}. A colour you set wins over the page colours mascot copies and over
Bootstrap variables, also in a \code{bslib} app. The package sets none of these
colour properties itself. When you set none, panels follow the page and the
restore button follows the character. When a mascot floats, it copies the
values it inherited from its original container; values set on the mascot
itself win.
\itemize{
\item \code{--mascot-panel-bg}: bubble, menu and tooltip backgrounds and tails.
Default: page background; otherwise \verb{#fff} in light mode, \verb{#212529} in dark.
\item \code{--mascot-panel-color}: panel text and minimise control.
Default: page text; otherwise \verb{#212529} in light mode, \verb{#f8f9fa} in dark.
\item \code{--mascot-panel-border}: panel and tail borders, bubble close border.
Default: page border; otherwise \verb{#dee2e6} in light mode, \verb{#495057} in dark.
\item \code{--mascot-restore-bg}: round restore button background.
Default: character body colour, or its first colour if absent.
\item \code{--mascot-restore-fg}: restore button text, border and focus outline.
Default: character outline colour, or its first colour if absent.
\item \code{--mascot-restore-glow}: restore button glow on hover or keyboard focus.
Default: the character's accent colour (its secondary brand colour, or \code{rim}), then
its main colour, then its first colour.
\item \code{--mascot-z-index}: floating mascot's stacking order.
Default: \code{1031}, above Bootstrap fixed navigation bars and below overlay
panels and modals. A supplied value wins over this default.
}
}

